# Chronology intervals: rule facem-chron-1. Century N spans the years (N-1)*100 to N*100. Within a century: first half = first 50 years, second half = last 50, first third = first 33, second quarter = years 25 to 50, end or late = last 25 years, beginning or early = first 25 years, mid = the year 50. A range takes the start of its first part and the end of its last part; a slash joins both parts. A year number stands for itself. '?', '(?)' and '(+)' are dropped and reported as uncertain.

